---
number: 625
title: I Wash’d My Hands This Morning
author: Lucinda M. Beal Bateman
composer: James Holmes Rosecrans
sp_category: "40"
topic: Children
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
I wash’d my hands this morning,
O very clean and bright,
And lent them both to Jesus,
To work for Him till night.

[chorus]
Little feet, be careful,
Where you take me to,
Anything for Jesus,
Only let me do.

[verse 2]
I told my ears to listen
Quite closely all day thro’,
For any act of kindness,
Such little hands can do.

[chorus]
Little feet, be careful,
Where you take me to,
Anything for Jesus,
Only let me do.

[verse 3]
My eyes are set to watch them
About their work or play,
To keep them out of mischief,
For Jesus’ sake all day.

[chorus]
Little feet, be careful,
Where you take me to,
Anything for Jesus,
Only let me do.
